WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.390 --> 00:00:04.270
The holidays are here in full swing, which
gives you two options: spend your evenings

00:00:04.270 --> 00:00:08.310
with family and loved ones, or hide away from
those weird relatives and catch up on all

00:00:08.310 --> 00:00:10.380
of Netflix's newest TV shows and movies.

00:00:10.580 --> 00:00:15.120
This December, you can definitely expect plenty
of holiday themed movies to hit the service,

00:00:15.360 --> 00:00:15.980
but that's not all.

00:00:16.140 --> 00:00:21.020
Here's a breakdown of everything you'd be
crazy to miss on Netflix in December 2017,

00:00:21.040 --> 00:00:22.540
starting with the Netflix originals.

00:00:23.260 --> 00:00:24.500
Dark: Season 1

00:00:25.000 --> 00:00:28.939
When two kids go missing in a small German
town, their families are plunged into a mystery

00:00:28.940 --> 00:00:30.200
that goes back decades.

00:00:30.380 --> 00:00:33.920
That's the premise for Dark, a German-language
Netflix original series.

00:00:34.160 --> 00:00:39.020
The morose atmosphere and flat color palette
showcased in the trailer evoke immediate comparisons

00:00:39.020 --> 00:00:42.920
to Stranger Things, although we're hoping
the 10-episode first season goes in a new

00:00:42.920 --> 00:00:45.860
direction and delivers something wholly original.

00:00:46.000 --> 00:00:47.960
Dark premieres on December 1st.

00:00:48.280 --> 00:00:49.360
Easy: Season 2

00:00:49.940 --> 00:00:54.280
An all-star cast is slated to appear in the
second season of Netflix's anthology series,

00:00:54.280 --> 00:00:54.780
Easy.

00:00:55.020 --> 00:00:59.200
Marc Maron, Dave Franco, and Aubrey Plaza
are just a few of the names showing up in

00:00:59.210 --> 00:01:03.520
the new season, and series creator Joe Swanberg
is again taking over writing and directing

00:01:03.520 --> 00:01:06.280
duties for each of the second season's eight
episodes.

00:01:06.500 --> 00:01:08.680
The entire season premieres on December 1st.

00:01:09.280 --> 00:01:10.360
My Happy Family

00:01:10.940 --> 00:01:15.020
Sundance darling My Happy Family is getting
a Netflix-exclusive release on the first of

00:01:15.020 --> 00:01:15.520
the month.

00:01:15.740 --> 00:01:19.780
The Georgian film starts with three generations
of a tight-knit family living in a single

00:01:19.790 --> 00:01:24.390
home, only for their lives to be flipped upside
down when 52-year-old Manara makes a shocking

00:01:24.390 --> 00:01:25.900
announcement: she's moving out.

00:01:26.360 --> 00:01:30.400
Tender and emotional, My Happy Family paints
a subtle portrait of what it means to leave

00:01:30.409 --> 00:01:34.580
everything you know, and the struggle to cope
with the fact that your happy family is really

00:01:34.580 --> 00:01:35.520
anything but.

00:01:36.180 --> 00:01:36.680
Voyeur

00:01:37.640 --> 00:01:39.240
True crime has never been so intimate.

00:01:39.480 --> 00:01:45.220
This Netflix original documentary is an adaptation
of 2016's The Voyeur's Motel, a nonfiction

00:01:45.229 --> 00:01:49.759
account centered on Gerald Foos, a motel owner
who installed special grates in his motel's

00:01:49.760 --> 00:01:52.840
rooms that would allow him to spy on his guests
without their knowledge.

00:01:53.060 --> 00:01:56.860
The book was written by journalist Gay Talese,
who also stars in the documentary.

00:01:57.140 --> 00:02:01.440
The film rights were actually purchased by
Steven Spielberg in 2016, but plans for his

00:02:01.450 --> 00:02:05.549
feature film were shelved following news that
Netflix was producing a documentary on the

00:02:05.549 --> 00:02:06.049
subject.

00:02:06.100 --> 00:02:08.960
Take a peep when Voyeur drops on December
1st.

00:02:09.280 --> 00:02:11.100
Craig Ferguson: Tickle Fight

00:02:11.660 --> 00:02:15.920
Longtime Late Late Show host Craig Ferguson
is landing on Netflix with an all-new comedy

00:02:15.920 --> 00:02:16.860
stand-up special.

00:02:17.220 --> 00:02:21.480
This will mark Ferguson's second special on
the streaming service, following his 2013

00:02:21.680 --> 00:02:23.660
special Craig Ferguson: I'm Here to Help.

00:02:23.970 --> 00:02:27.920
If Tickle Fight takes the same cues as his
prior special, it's bound to be hilarious,

00:02:27.920 --> 00:02:29.660
timely, and completely irreverent.

00:02:29.880 --> 00:02:33.840
"When a smart woman wants to stay married
to a guy after the wedding she fattens him

00:02:33.840 --> 00:02:35.140
up a little bit, not too much!

00:02:35.640 --> 00:02:39.160
Just enough to slow the 'f----- down in case
he gets any ideas."

00:02:39.360 --> 00:02:40.800
Look for it on December 5th.

00:02:41.120 --> 00:02:42.400
El Camino Christmas

00:02:42.700 --> 00:02:46.620
When five people are taken hostage in a liquor
store on Christmas Eve, the holidays quickly

00:02:46.620 --> 00:02:47.700
turn into a nightmare.

00:02:48.200 --> 00:02:53.600
El Camino Christmas stars Tim Allen, Dax Shepard,
Jessica Alba, and Vincent D'Onofrio in a comedic

00:02:53.600 --> 00:02:57.160
crime story about one man's search for his
father that goes horribly wrong.

00:02:57.500 --> 00:03:01.340
The movie's based on a script by Ted Melfi,
who wrote and directed the Oscar-nominated

00:03:01.340 --> 00:03:03.320
Hidden Figures as well as St. Vincent.

00:03:03.600 --> 00:03:04.800
Check it out on December 8th.

00:03:05.700 --> 00:03:06.860
The Crown: Season 2

00:03:07.440 --> 00:03:12.060
Netflix's award-winning historical drama The
Crown is gearing up for Season 2, continuing

00:03:12.060 --> 00:03:16.450
the story of a young Queen Elizabeth The Second,
her marriage to Prince Philip, and her struggles

00:03:16.450 --> 00:03:19.660
to maintain order in a constantly changing
world scarred by war.

00:03:19.989 --> 00:03:23.480
The second season will see the return of the
main cast, along with the addition of Dexter's

00:03:23.489 --> 00:03:26.189
Michael C. Hall in the role of John F. Kennedy.

00:03:26.189 --> 00:03:27.520
The wait is over on December 8th.

00:03:28.540 --> 00:03:30.040
Judd Apatow: The Return

00:03:30.500 --> 00:03:35.080
Despite being the man behind the camera on
countless smash hit comedies—including The

00:03:35.099 --> 00:03:39.210
40-Year-Old-Virgin, Knocked Up, and Trainwreck—you
don't often get a chance to see Judd Apatow

00:03:39.210 --> 00:03:40.220
in front of the camera.

00:03:40.480 --> 00:03:44.800
That's all changing with Judd Apatow: The
Return, a stand-up special that sees Apatow

00:03:44.800 --> 00:03:48.000
step on the stage for the first time in over
25 years.

00:03:48.260 --> 00:03:49.620
Look for it on December 12.

00:03:50.380 --> 00:03:51.920
Erased: Season 1

00:03:52.160 --> 00:03:56.680
Based on the manga of the same name, Erased
is an all-new live-action show about a man

00:03:56.680 --> 00:04:01.000
who discovers that he has the ability to travel
back in time to prevent past tragedies from

00:04:01.000 --> 00:04:01.500
happening.

00:04:01.840 --> 00:04:05.960
This will mark the third adaption of the manga,
the previous two being an anime series that

00:04:05.960 --> 00:04:11.020
premiered in January 2016 and a live-action
film that screened in Japan in March 2016.

00:04:11.180 --> 00:04:16.320
Get ready for an all-new telling of the story
when Erased: Season 1 drops on December 15th.

00:04:16.920 --> 00:04:18.560
The Ranch: Part 4

00:04:19.200 --> 00:04:24.100
The Ashton Kutcher-led sitcom The Ranch has
been an audience favorite since its 2016 premiere,

00:04:24.100 --> 00:04:26.620
although critics haven't been particularly
kind to the show.

00:04:26.860 --> 00:04:30.880
The story centers on Colt Bennett, a football
player who couldn't cut it in the big time,

00:04:30.880 --> 00:04:33.500
so he's forced to move back to the family
ranch in Colorado.

00:04:33.680 --> 00:04:37.460
As they did with the latest season of Fuller
House, Netflix released each season of The

00:04:37.460 --> 00:04:39.180
Ranch broken up into two parts.

00:04:39.540 --> 00:04:43.780
Part 4, which is the second part of Season
2, hits Netflix on December 15th.

00:04:44.180 --> 00:04:46.160
Ultimate Beastmaster: Season 2

00:04:46.400 --> 00:04:50.600
Who doesn't love watching contestants bash
their way through a seemingly impossible obstacle

00:04:50.600 --> 00:04:51.100
course?

00:04:51.380 --> 00:04:56.060
In the spirit of Ninja Warrior, Ultimate Beastmaster
pits elite athletes against the clock as they

00:04:56.060 --> 00:04:59.360
struggle to make it past a series of gruelling
physical challenges.

00:04:59.600 --> 00:05:03.900
Season 2 arrives on December 15th, so sit
back and live vicariously through the pain

00:05:03.940 --> 00:05:04.680
of others.

00:05:05.140 --> 00:05:05.860
The American way.

00:05:06.740 --> 00:05:07.380
Wormwood

00:05:08.040 --> 00:05:12.440
The first teaser for Netflix's hotly anticipated
show Wormwood dropped way back in August,

00:05:12.440 --> 00:05:14.500
and the hype has only grown since then.

00:05:14.960 --> 00:05:20.240
Part fiction and part documentary, the show
dives into the dark history of the CIA's infamous

00:05:20.250 --> 00:05:26.220
MK Ultra experiments, focusing specifically
on one scientist who was involved in the secretive

00:05:26.220 --> 00:05:26.780
operation.

00:05:27.280 --> 00:05:31.440
From Oscar-winning director Errol Morris,
Wormwood promises a paranoia-fueled journey

00:05:31.440 --> 00:05:34.820
into the dark heart of government conspiracy.

00:05:34.820 --> 00:05:37.280
Settle in for the six-part miniseries on December
15th.

00:05:37.760 --> 00:05:39.660
Hello, My Twenties!: Season 2

00:05:40.200 --> 00:05:45.080
Also known as Age of Youth in its origin country
of South Korea, this comedy-drama series follows

00:05:45.090 --> 00:05:49.620
five college-age girls from different walks
of life who live in the same house.

00:05:49.620 --> 00:05:53.310
If you haven't seen the first season yet,
now would be a good time to go back and watch

00:05:53.310 --> 00:05:55.800
it, because Season 2 arrives on December 18th.

00:05:56.780 --> 00:05:58.280
Russell Howard: Recalibrate

00:05:58.660 --> 00:06:03.310
British comedian Russell Howard has been selling
out shows across the UK, and now he's slated

00:06:03.310 --> 00:06:07.560
to star in a Netflix-exclusive stand-up special,
Russel Howard: Recalibrate.

00:06:07.800 --> 00:06:09.620
Queue up the laughs on December 19th.

00:06:10.520 --> 00:06:11.960
The Indian Detective: Season 1

00:06:12.260 --> 00:06:16.400
Starring Russell Peters, Christina Cole, and
William Shatner, The Indian Detective is a

00:06:16.401 --> 00:06:20.810
Canadian crime comedy about a Toronto cop
who gets drawn into a murder investigation

00:06:20.810 --> 00:06:22.180
while visiting his family in India.

00:06:22.740 --> 00:06:27.060
The first season consists of four episodes,
all of which are slated to arrive on Netflix

00:06:27.060 --> 00:06:28.100
on December 19th.

00:06:28.660 --> 00:06:30.700
La Casa de Papel: Season 1

00:06:31.120 --> 00:06:35.520
This heist thriller made waves with its Spanish
television premiere, and now Netflix is rolling

00:06:35.520 --> 00:06:38.000
it out to international audiences on December
20th.

00:06:38.280 --> 00:06:42.490
The title translates to "The House of Paper,"
and the story follows eight bank robbers planning

00:06:42.490 --> 00:06:44.760
to pull off the biggest heist Spain has ever
seen.

00:06:45.080 --> 00:06:50.140
If you don't mind the subtitles, you can binge
the entire first season when La Casa de Papel

00:06:50.140 --> 00:06:51.080
drops later this month.

00:06:52.300 --> 00:06:53.660
Peaky Blinders: Season 4

00:06:54.380 --> 00:06:59.340
Ever since its 2013 premiere, Peaky Blinders
has steadily gained more and more attention,

00:06:59.350 --> 00:07:03.730
with critics praising the show's characters,
acting, and story, among many other elements

00:07:03.730 --> 00:07:07.340
that come together to make this powerful drama
as effective as it is.

00:07:08.400 --> 00:07:12.520
"I want you to be alive after your entire
family is passed."

00:07:13.280 --> 00:07:18.080
Whether you've been waiting eagerly for Season
4 or are just now starting the entire series,

00:07:18.080 --> 00:07:21.780
mark your calendar for December 21st and get
ready for the brand new season.

00:07:22.620 --> 00:07:23.320
Bright

00:07:24.220 --> 00:07:28.480
Written by Max Landis and directed by David
Ayer, Bright is a Netflix original film starring

00:07:28.480 --> 00:07:33.630
Will Smith as Daryl Ward, an LAPD officer
who has to team up with an Orc to stop an

00:07:33.630 --> 00:07:36.090
evil force threatening to destroy the world.

00:07:36.090 --> 00:07:41.130
Equal parts crime thriller and fantasy, Bright
promises a take on the buddy cop trope that'll

00:07:41.130 --> 00:07:43.060
definitely be unique, if nothing else.

00:07:43.500 --> 00:07:45.180
Look for it on December 22nd.

00:07:46.000 --> 00:07:48.380
Fuller House: Season 3, New Episodes

00:07:49.120 --> 00:07:53.180
Ever since Netflix released the first part
of Season 3 of Fuller House in September,

00:07:53.300 --> 00:07:56.200
fans have been eagerly anticipating the season's
second half.

00:07:56.200 --> 00:07:58.640
"But… our boarding passes say we are flying
coach."

00:07:59.360 --> 00:08:01.180
"Coach… bmmmm"

00:08:01.420 --> 00:08:05.660
And the wait will soon be over—the final
nine episodes of Season 3 are slated for a

00:08:05.660 --> 00:08:10.260
December 22nd release, just in time to tune
in with the whole family over the holidays.

00:08:11.080 --> 00:08:12.640
The Toys That Made Us: Season 1

00:08:12.920 --> 00:08:17.740
Get ready for a blast from the past with The
Toys That Made Us, Netflix's new nostalgia-driven

00:08:17.740 --> 00:08:22.100
series that looks back on the iconic toys
of the '80s and '90s and the stories behind

00:08:22.100 --> 00:08:22.600
them.

00:08:22.800 --> 00:08:24.600
If you're thinking He-Man, G.I.

00:08:24.600 --> 00:08:26.560
Joe, and Transformers, you're on the right
track.

00:08:26.940 --> 00:08:28.740
"It's two against one."

00:08:28.740 --> 00:08:30.460
"Wrong Boneface.

00:08:30.460 --> 00:08:32.770
It's two agains two!"

00:08:32.770 --> 00:08:35.680
"Moss Man fooled you, Yarrrrrr!"

00:08:35.860 --> 00:08:40.620
The show premieres on December 22, just in
time to make you rethink your holiday wish

00:08:40.620 --> 00:08:41.120
list.

00:08:41.680 --> 00:08:43.040
Cable Girls: Season 2

00:08:43.380 --> 00:08:48.800
Set in 1928, Cable Girls tells the story of
four women who get jobs at a state-of-the-art

00:08:48.810 --> 00:08:52.930
telecom company in Madrid, focusing on their
troubled past lives and the relationships

00:08:52.930 --> 00:08:55.280
that emerge as they finally get a new lease
on life.

00:08:55.740 --> 00:08:59.900
Season 1 served up plenty of hard-hitting
drama, and chances are fans can expect more

00:08:59.900 --> 00:09:03.420
of the same from the second season, which
will be available for streaming on Christmas

00:09:03.420 --> 00:09:03.920
day.

00:09:04.540 --> 00:09:06.000
Todd Barry: Spicy Honey

00:09:06.400 --> 00:09:10.840
Veteran stand-up comic Todd Barry is joining
the Netflix line-up this December with Todd

00:09:10.840 --> 00:09:15.720
Barry: Spicy Honey, a new comedy special that
promises more of Barry's signature dry style

00:09:15.720 --> 00:09:18.710
coupled with brand-new material that fans
are sure to love.

00:09:18.710 --> 00:09:21.020
Tune in on December 26 for all the laughs.

00:09:21.220 --> 00:09:22.540
It's the day after Christmas.

00:09:22.540 --> 00:09:23.220
What else are you going to do?

00:09:23.920 --> 00:09:25.020
Travelers: Season 2

00:09:25.700 --> 00:09:30.620
Once you're done burning through Future Man
and 11.22.63 over on Hulu, head back to Netflix

00:09:30.620 --> 00:09:33.880
to get your time-travel fix with the Season
2 premiere of Travelers.

00:09:33.940 --> 00:09:39.000
Created by Brad Wright, the man behind Stargate
SG-1 and Stargate: Atlantis, Travelers follows

00:09:39.010 --> 00:09:43.650
four people hundreds of years in the future
who transport their minds back into new bodies

00:09:43.650 --> 00:09:47.860
in the 21st century in an attempt to prevent
the dystopia that will become of our world.

00:09:48.080 --> 00:09:52.360
Season 2 of the sci-fi drama will be released
globally on Netflix on December 26th.

00:09:53.460 --> 00:09:56.760
Bill Nye Saves the World: Season 2: Part 1

00:09:57.520 --> 00:10:01.360
The first season of Bill Nye Saves the World
was met with a storm of controversy.

00:10:01.700 --> 00:10:05.900
Most people disliked the content and the political
nature of the show, while others were just

00:10:05.900 --> 00:10:09.410
upset that Nye didn't seem to be the same
Science Guy we loved from the '90s.

00:10:09.580 --> 00:10:10.880
"Good heavens!

00:10:10.880 --> 00:10:13.740
It's Bill Nye the Science Guy!"

00:10:14.000 --> 00:10:18.140
Either way, the majority of the show's audience
found something to hate, and the Season 2

00:10:18.150 --> 00:10:21.920
announcement trailer made the unusual decision
to highlight the negative reactions to the

00:10:21.920 --> 00:10:22.500
first season.

00:10:22.780 --> 00:10:24.240
Because that always helps.

00:10:24.560 --> 00:10:29.440
Love it or hate it, Bill Nye Saves the World
is returning, with the second season landing

00:10:29.440 --> 00:10:30.580
on December 29th.

00:10:31.520 --> 00:10:33.000
La Mante: Season 1

00:10:33.380 --> 00:10:37.720
Originally aired in France, La Mante, or "The
Mantis," is a psychological drama about the

00:10:37.740 --> 00:10:42.260
search for a vicious criminal who's recreating
the crimes perpetrated by The Mantis, a psychopath

00:10:42.260 --> 00:10:44.260
who operated 20 years previously.

00:10:45.220 --> 00:10:48.920
The police have no choice but to turn to The
Mantis for help tracking down the new murderer.

00:10:49.560 --> 00:10:52.280
The six-episode miniseries premieres on December
29th.

00:10:52.780 --> 00:10:54.480
Dave Chappelle: Equanimity

00:10:55.060 --> 00:10:58.760
Netflix is ending the year with a new comedy
special from Dave Chappelle, his third to

00:10:58.760 --> 00:11:00.140
hit Netflix in 2017.

00:11:00.600 --> 00:11:04.760
Netflix describes Dave Chappelle: Equanimity
as a return "to his roots."

00:11:04.760 --> 00:11:08.540
After Chappelle's long hiatus from the spotlight
and some mixed reviews on his previous Netflix

00:11:08.540 --> 00:11:11.980
specials, we can only hope his newest outing
delivers on that promise.

00:11:12.080 --> 00:11:13.780
Check it out when it lands on New Year's Eve.

00:11:19.360 --> 00:11:19.860
"Do me!

00:11:20.240 --> 00:11:21.080
Do me next."

00:11:21.560 --> 00:11:24.820
That does it for the Netflix originals coming
out in December 2017.

00:11:24.940 --> 00:11:27.380
Now let's look at everything else that's hitting
the streaming service.

00:11:28.240 --> 00:11:29.160
New movies

00:11:29.820 --> 00:11:33.100
We know, government plots and space battles
don't usually come to mind when you think

00:11:33.280 --> 00:11:36.990
of the holidays, but Netflix is ushering in
a few action movies this month that will give

00:11:36.990 --> 00:11:38.580
you a break from the snow and sleet.

00:11:38.840 --> 00:11:43.530
V for Vendetta will be available on December
1, followed by Guardians of the Galaxy Vol.

00:11:43.530 --> 00:11:44.300
2 on the 5th.

00:11:44.800 --> 00:11:46.700
"I'm Mary Poppins, yall!"

00:11:47.000 --> 00:11:49.880
Netflix is also doubling down on classic comedy
films.

00:11:49.900 --> 00:11:55.060
Relive the past with both original Ace Ventura
films, Hitch, Nacho Libre, and While You Were

00:11:55.070 --> 00:11:56.470
Sleeping on December 1st.

00:11:56.470 --> 00:11:59.540
And if those get you in the mood for family
movie night, you're in luck.

00:11:59.880 --> 00:12:04.400
From Trolls Holiday Special, landing on December
6th, to all three films in The Santa Clause

00:12:04.400 --> 00:12:08.620
franchise on December 12th, you won't be able
to escape the festivities this year.

00:12:08.620 --> 00:12:09.300
Even if you try.

00:12:09.620 --> 00:12:13.240
Of course, the holidays aren't all about love
and family—sometimes you need a dose of

00:12:13.240 --> 00:12:15.600
betrayal and revenge, just to round things
out.

00:12:15.890 --> 00:12:20.740
On December 1st, Netflix is adding drama classics
like 8 Mile and Full Metal Jacket to their

00:12:20.740 --> 00:12:24.420
lineup, followed by Nicolas Winding Refn's
Pusher on December 27.

00:12:24.660 --> 00:12:29.360
In the thriller genre, Netflix is adding 2003's
Dreamcatcher, starring Tom Jane.

00:12:29.520 --> 00:12:35.060
Then, on December 23, tune in for Creep 2,
the sequel to the 2014 underground hit.

00:12:35.060 --> 00:12:38.920
Mark Duplass returns as everyone's favorite
psycho, with Patrick Bryce back in the director's

00:12:38.920 --> 00:12:39.420
chair.

00:12:39.620 --> 00:12:43.860
Finally, the documentary line-up is definitely
cause for excitement, with the addition Planet

00:12:43.870 --> 00:12:48.940
Earth II, the 2016 follow-up to BBC's award-winning
2006 nature series.

00:12:48.940 --> 00:12:52.130
If you're a fan of nature docs, get ready
to experience the world like you've never

00:12:52.130 --> 00:12:55.000
seen it before—again—on December 25th.

00:12:55.280 --> 00:13:00.120
Other documentaries to watch this month include
The Farthest: Voyager in Space, a PBS production

00:13:00.120 --> 00:13:01.800
about the Voyager probes.

00:13:01.960 --> 00:13:06.240
Check it out on December 1st, and then look
for Discovering Bigfoot and Freeway: Crack

00:13:06.240 --> 00:13:07.760
in the System on December 15th.

00:13:08.860 --> 00:13:09.760
New Television

00:13:10.280 --> 00:13:13.560
